%% Module 3 job state machine, including POST /v1/cancel (Phase 3 close-out C1).
%% The older drawing, send_byo_job_lifecycle_states.svg, predates `cancelled`; this file is the current one.
%% Source of truth for the states: the send_byo.job_state enum (send_byo_0003, plus 'cancelled' at send_byo_0056),
%% published live in GET /v1/describe -> vocabularies.job_state.
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> queued: POST /v1/run (one job per job_item_id)

    queued --> assigned: the dispatcher claims it (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED; a job flagged cancel_requested_at is never claimed)
    assigned --> sending: an eligible account is consumed and the job is pushed to a worker
    sending --> sent: the worker reports SMTP accepted (provider_message_id set)
    sending --> bounced: the worker reports a permanent recipient rejection (550)

    sending --> queued: a retryable failure (4xx, timeout, throttle, auth) requeues with backoff
    assigned --> queued: no account or no worker (requeue) / lease expired (reclaim)
    sending --> queued: dead worker / lease expired (reclaim)

    queued --> failed: every account the user has is blocked (exhaustion sweep), or campaign expiry at enforce

    queued --> cancelled: POST /v1/cancel (an item not yet claimed)
    assigned --> cancelled: a flagged item whose claim falls through (requeue becomes cancelled, never queued again)
    sending --> cancelled: a flagged item whose attempt FAILS, or whose worker died (the guard turns the requeue into cancelled)

    sent --> [*]
    bounced --> [*]
    failed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]

    note right of cancelled
        Terminal. Never sent (a flagged item that is already
        assigned/sending FINISHES: sent or bounced, reported once).
        A second POST /v1/cancel changes nothing.
    end note
